<% identity = Rails.configuration.x.foundation %>
<article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-6 leading-relaxed">
  <header>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-md-on-surface-variant">
      Version <%= Foundation::Legal.privacy_label %>
      &middot; Last updated <%= Foundation::Legal::PRIVACY_UPDATED_ON.iso8601 %>
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 rounded-md border border-md-tertiary bg-md-tertiary-container px-4 py-3 text-sm text-md-on-tertiary-container">
      Demo preview: this deployment is test-only. Review this policy with
      qualified counsel before a production launch and add the data
      controller's legal entity and address here.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      This policy explains how the operator of
      <%= identity[:application_name] %> ("we") handles personal data when you
      use the Service at https://<%= identity[:domain] %>. Until the operator
      is named for production, this demo runs as a test preview. For anything
      in this policy, contact
      <%= mail_to identity[:legal_email], nil, class: "underline underline-offset-2" %>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">2. Data we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>Messages.</strong> The message text you post to the wall, an
      optional name, and the time it was posted. These are public and
      displayed to everyone who visits the page.</p>
    <p><strong>Technical data.</strong> Server logs with IP address, browser
      user agent, requested pages, and timestamps, kept briefly for security
      and debugging.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">3. Why we use it</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
      <li>to provide the Service: displaying the messages you post on the wall;</li>
      <li>to secure it: preventing abuse, spam, and denial-of-service;</li>
      <li>to comply with legal obligations if any apply.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell personal data and do not use it for advertising.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">4. Sharing and retention</h2>
    <p>
      Messages are shared publicly by design — that is the point of a
      guestbook. Technical logs are shared only with our hosting processor
      (Holodex) under a data-processing relationship, and are retained only
      as long as needed for security and debugging. You can ask to have a
      message you posted removed by contacting
      <%= mail_to identity[:support_email], nil, class: "underline underline-offset-2" %>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">5. Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can choose not to post a message. Because messages are anonymous
      (an optional name is not an account), a request to remove one relies on
      you identifying it for us. The demo deployment is reset daily, so
      anything posted is not retained long-term.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">6. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For questions about this policy, contact
      <%= mail_to identity[:legal_email], nil, class: "underline underline-offset-2" %>.
    </p>
  </section>
</article>
